sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Confirm request
    participant E as Expiry worker
    participant H as PostgreSQL hold row
    participant V as PostgreSQL capacity row
    participant O as Outbox
    participant B as Broker
    participant D as Inbox consumer

    par Confirm-vs-Expire race
        C->>H: Begin transaction; verify Active and DB time < expires_at
        C->>H: Conditional Active -> Confirmed
        C->>V: held - units; confirmed + units
        C->>O: Insert BookingConfirmed atomically
    and
        E->>H: Begin transaction; verify Active and DB time >= expires_at
        E->>H: Conditional Active -> Expired
        E->>V: held - units
        E->>O: Insert CapacityHoldExpired atomically
    end
    Note over H,V: Row locks and conditional state transition allow one terminal winner

    O->>B: Publish pending message
    B-->>O: Transient failure
    O->>O: Keep unprocessed; increment attempt/error
    O->>B: Retry after next poll
    B->>D: At-least-once delivery with stable MessageId
    D->>D: INSERT inbox ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
    D->>D: Apply one downstream effect transactionally
    B->>D: Duplicate delivery
    D-->>D: No-op because inbox MessageId already exists
